include [] for cleanliness. Hmm, that adds bulk. I'll include \"footnote_markers\": [] only... okay include for all, fine.\n\nActually to reduce size, I'll omit footnote_markers when empty. The rules say record marker when value references footnote. Omitting empty is fine.\n\nmodel_level entries:\n\n1. {\"attribute\": \"q3\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [{model/value ×6}]}\n2. {\"attribute\": \"nominal_diameter\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", values: 15,15,20,20,25,25}\n3. {\"attribute\": \"connection_thread\", \"unit_symbol\": null, values: \"G3/4\\\"\", \"G3/4\\\"\", \"G1\", \"G1\", \"G1¼\\\"\", \"G1¼\\\"\"}\n4. {\"attribute\": \"length\", \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", values: {min,max} ×6}\n5. {\"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\", values: \"Δp40\"×5, \"Δp63\"}\n6. {\"attribute\": \"q3_q1_ratio_options\", values: \"800; 400; 250\" (models 1-3), \"1600; 800; 400; 250\" (models 4-6)}\n\nHmm — for q3_q1_ratio_options, maybe better attribute name \"q3_q1\". And values as strings \"800, 400, 250\". I'll name it \"q3_q1_ratio\" with string list values and add a note in matrix_tables description. Values like \"800; 400; 250\" (semicolon-separated to match source).\n\nmatrix_tables:\n\nTable 1:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Metrological specifications\",\n  \"columns\": [\"model\", \"nominal_diameter\", \"q3\", \"q3_q1_ratio_options\", \"q2_q1\", \"q4_q3\", \"pressure_loss_class\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, \"mm\", \"m³/h\", null, null, null, null],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"model\": \"DN15_Q3=1.6\", \"nominal_diameter\": 15, \"q3\": 1.6, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"800; 400; 250\", \"q2_q1\": 1.6, \"q4_q3\": 1.25, \"pressure_loss_class\": \"Δp40\"},\n    {\"model\": \"DN15_Q3=2.5\", \"nominal_diameter\": 15, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"800; 400; 250\", ...},\n    {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=2.5\", \"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"800; 400; 250\", ...},\n    {\"model\": \"DN20_Q3=4.0\", \"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"1600; 800; 400; 250\", ...},\n    {\"model\": \"DN25_Q3=4.0\", \"nominal_diameter\": 25, \"q3\": 4.0, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"1600; 800; 400; 250\", ...},\n    {\"model\": \"DN25_Q3=6.3\", \"nominal_diameter\": 25, \"q3\": 6.3, \"q3_q1_ratio_options\": \"1600; 800; 400; 250\", \"pressure_loss_class\": \"Δp63\"}\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Six certified size/ratio columns. Nominal diameters 15/20/25 span two columns each; ratio options per column group as transcribed (first three columns: 800/400/250; last three: 1600/800/400/250).\",\n  \"footnotes\": []\n}\n\nTable 2:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Installation specifications\",\n  \"columns\": [\"model\", \"connection_thread\", \"length\", \"min_straight_inlet_pipe_length\", \"min_straight_outlet_pipe_length\", \"flow_profile_sensitivity_class\", \"flow_conditioner\", \"mounting\", \"protection_degree\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, null, \"mm\", \"mm\", \"mm\", null, null, null, null],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"model\": \"DN15_Q3=1.6\", \"connection_thread\": \"G3/4\\\"\", \"length\": {\"min\": 110, \"max\": 165}, ...},\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n\nMaybe fold table 2 into matrix only (since model_level already carries thread/length). It's fine to have both.\n\ntest_reports:\n[\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V088-26\", \"date\": \"2026-07-14\", \"pages\": 47, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"194400-061/2022\", \"date\": null, \"pages\": null, \"role\": \"test_report\"},  — associated with ER-V061-22. Should I link? No field for link; fine.\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V061-22\", \"date\": \"2022-10-24\", \"pages\": 43, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V029-20\", \"pages\": 93, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"8551-PT-E0118-21\", \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6011-PT-SW004-22\", \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V015-23\", \"pages\": 134, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P0007-24\", \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6011-PT-SW004-24\", \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-ER-V049-24\", \"pages\": 99, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"6015-PT-P0025-24\", \"role\": \"test_report\"},\n  {\"id\": \"0511-UL-V088-26\", \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n]\n\nOmit null fields rather than including nulls? Rule 8: omit if not present. I'll omit date/pages where unknown.\n\nOrder: maybe group ERs first then their sub-reports. Fine.\n\nrevision_history: [{\"revision\": \"0\", \"date\": \"2026-07-20\", \"changes\": \"Issuing certificate (no prior revisions)\"}]\n\nCertificate \"scheme\": \"A\".\n\nNote the certificate number: \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-26.03\". Good.\n\nDescription text: \"The water meters type WMP are ultrasonic water meters designed to measure, memorise and display the volume at metering conditions of water passing through the measurement transducer. They consist of a brass body with connecting screw threads, one pair of ultrasonic transducers and an electronic indicating device with LCD display (volume resolution 0.000 001 m³). Battery powered (3.6 V DC), without buttons or communication interfaces. Software separation with CRC and SW version of the legally relevant part displayed on the LCD. Can be installed in horizontal position with indicating device at top or at side, and vertical position with flow from bottom to top.\"\n\nEscape the ³ fine in JSON.\n\nOne more check — \"Q₃/Q₁ | 800; 400; 250 / 1600; 800; 400; 250 (per column)\". I've decided the grouping. In the matrix description I'll note the transcription.\n\nAlso \"Temperature class T30 or T50\": max admissible temperature 50 °C listed. Fine.\n\nDo I include \"water_pressure_class\": MAP16 AND max_admissible_pressure 1.6 MPa — both yes.\n\nAlso \"Q₃/Q₁\" attribute name: \"q3_q1_ratio\". Values as string options.\n\nModel ids — let me finalize: \"DN15_Q3=1.6\" style. Also give label: \"DN15, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h\".\n\nLet me write the final JSON. Ensure numbers like 4.0 → write as 4.0 (JSON will parse as 4). Fine.\n\nConnection thread with inch marks: \"G3/4\\\"\" — in JSON string: \"G3\\/4\\\"\" no need to escape slash. Write \"G3/4\\\"\". The ¼ char: \"G1¼\\\"\". OK.\n\nArrows ↑ → fine in JSON (UTF-8).\n\nΔ char fine.\n\nLet me write it out.",
